{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1172534-1001-paths-of-seekings","id":1172534,"title":"1001 Paths of Seekings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-01T21:56:47-08:00","id":1172534,"title":"1001 Paths of Seekings","content":"So im looking for ideas for potential seekings and for different scenario ideas involving suchs. any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:35:22-08:00","id":1172546,"title":"","content":"1) Taking place on a theater stage, where people from the mage's life are actors. The Seekings run like scenes in a stage play, and the mage completes them by assuming the correct role.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) The mage's childhood home is fused into the hallways of a vast airship, and populated by passengers in dress akin to the early 20th century. The airship is also locked in an endless loop of tragedy, where everyone dies from murdering each other, followed by the airship crashing. Each Seeking involves unraveling an aspect of the overall mystery on the ship, saving one of the victims, and getting closer to averting the vessel's doom. If the mage can ever prevent the disaster from happening, they will Ascend as the airship flies beyond the limits of the otherwise perpetually overcast sky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T04:35:50-08:00","id":1173733,"title":"","content":"Here are a few of the seekings I've provided for all the players in the last game I ran.<br /> <br /> 3) Virtual Adept, Dynamic: Trapped in a strange room, black walls with neon lines. The room in a complete cube. On the table is a computer with the mage's mentor messaging them instructions on how to leave. The cube is one of a series of similar puzzle rooms, each with a different puzzle. Any time a puzzle is completed incorrectly, the floor will start to crumble, dropping the mage down a level. The messages advising the mage will always be incorrect, and following their advise will causing the floor to crumble. Going it alone is the only way to proceed. Right at the end, the mentor messages let the mage know that deeper in the maze, there is a golden pyramid that they need to retrieve before they leave. If they chose to go get it, then the floor will open up the moment they take it and the seeking is lost. If they chose to leave the maze empty handed, the messages will become more frantic until the mage openly defies their mentor, by which point leaving the maze will lead to passage.<br /> <br /> 4) Virtual Adept, Dynamic: Similar to 3) but with a different emphasis. The mage is in a videogame like maze, complete with pixel textures, low poly count, and a lot of stuttering frames. The text &quot;load theseus.exe appears in the top left corner of their vision. There is a computer on the desk open to a gamefaqs page, but it is chained to the wall and impossible to take with. Tied to the chain is a long spool of golden thread. The maze is long and nonsensical, filled with puzzles and labyrinthine turns that are impossible to figure out without the walkthrough, which has over 500 steps. The mage must figure out a way through the maze, using the golden thread to make their way back to the walkthrough between intervals. However, the further they go, the more taught the golden thread becomes, until it starts to get harder and harder to move. There is a strange elasticity to it, making it easier to get back to the computer room than to leave it. Eventually, the mage will find a puzzle the walkthrough ignores. Solving it on their own opens a new door which the golden thread will always be too taught to reach. They will have to let go of the thread and travel the rest of the path alone to pass the seeking.<br /> <br /> 5) Templar Knight, Primordial: They wake unto a scene of sheer destruction. The ruins of a city caught in a blazing inferno. In the distance, a dragon flies menacingly. Once it notices the mage, it heads towards them. The dragon is completely invincible from all physical and mystical attacks. The only way to harm it is to use its own quintessence against it. Prime 3 to absorb it, Prime 2 to fire it back. If the mage tries to attack the creature in any other way, they will slowly lose health levels. Once the 7th level is gone, the mage will be slain, and the seeking lost. If the mage successfully figures out how to defeat the dragon, then in death the dragon will change form to that of a man, a knight like himself. To recognise the power the prime promises and warns is to pass the seeking.<br /> <br /> 6) Hollow One, Dynamic: The mage considers himself a detective straight out of a film noir story. They used to be a cop who awakened shortly after pursuing a Jhor laden euthanatos and taking their life. This seeking forces them to confront the victim. It starts with them at a bar which seems both out of place, and yet familiar. The bar keeper is a friendly sort, someone the Mage feels they have known a long time despite only just meeting them. They get into conversation and soon the Mage opens up about his past. Every moment leading up to his awakening is replayed before him, he is certain there is no way to change it. When he finally gets to the confrontation with the Euthanatos mage, the bar scene fades away almost completly, and they find themselves taring straight at euthanatos. The exchange is carried out and the Mage must decide whether shooting them in the past was truly the best outcome. If the mage shoots, the seeking is lost, and they will return to the bar where they will drink themselves into a blackout. If the mage holds off, and admits that we acted rashly, that in the moment he made a bad decision, the seeking is won.<br /> ALTERNATIVE: The doors open behind the mage, and they hear their own voice call back to them. The mage is no longer themselves, but transformed into the long dead euthanatos, and they now staring down the barrel of their own gun. They must convince their past self there was another way or else be shot by their own hand.<br /> <br /> 7) Verbena, Primordial: The mage has the sword Excalibur as their avatar. They find themselves on a moor by a lake. A huge army is approaching. Beside them is a lake from which a glint of metal is seen. Around them the battle draws near, the loud sounds of angry charges growing closer with each passing second. The mage has no means to fight, but the metal in the lake calls to them. They will see it as a sword. The sword cannot be reached by magical means. The only way to get to it is to dive in. As the mage dives in, they will slowly drown as per normal drowning rules, bashing damage for every few moments under water. If the mage comes up for air, all progress is reversed, and the battle will draw much closer. If the mage attempts to do anything clever under the water, it will fail. The only way to reach the blade is to swim straight to it, only reaching it when the last health level is lost. The mage will faint and awaken on avalon where they will glimpse at the lady of the lake before returning to reality having succeeded. Failure is returning to the surface too often, and being slaughtered by the fighting armies.<br /> <br /> 8) Hermetic, Questing: The mage lost their parents to a ritual sacrifice when they were young. After witnessing their parents being burned at the stake in the woods, they were chased off by one of the cultists, and awakened after inadvertently conjuring a ring of flames to protect themselves. Their seeking brings them back to that woods, where a faint glow and cries of their name can be heard, leading them deeper and deeper. Once they arrive at the site of the ritual, they can see their parents tied up and calling to the mage. They can attempt to free them, but as they do so, they are assaulted by a cloaked figure with a dagger. If the figure's hood is removed, the mage will see their own face. If the mage speaks to them, the figure will respond with the same words in the same voice. As long as the mage is confrontational, so too will the figure respond in kind. If the mage lets the figure go, they will no longer be hostile, the seeking is passed and the Mage can have a small reunion with their parents before fading to black. If the mage instead tries to attack the figure, say by stabbing them in the chest, the mage will die from the same wound, the knife is now sticking out of their own chest, and the seeking is failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}